00:06:42.615 --> 00:06:46.623
(creepy music)

00:06:46.870 --> 00:06:50.750
The case file on The Ferryman shows many old
photos, but I think these are photos that

00:06:50.750 --> 00:06:54.340
Ed and Lorraine collected, not necessarily
snapshots that they took themselves.

00:06:54.340 --> 00:06:58.270
If you look at the clothes these people are
wearing, this guy has a big old Victorian

00:06:58.270 --> 00:07:02.259
bow-tie, and this lady, whose full portrait
we see in the behind-the-scenes content, similarly

00:07:02.259 --> 00:07:05.270
has a dress that matches what you might see
in Victorian times.

00:07:05.270 --> 00:07:08.990
The bodies are not yet decomposed, so these
pictures were probably taken well before Ed

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:10.199
and Lorraine were born.

00:07:10.199 --> 00:07:13.770
Another photo, of a candle in the grass next
to some runes and what looks like a witch

00:07:13.770 --> 00:07:18.590
totem is labeled March 1921, again, a good
five years before Ed was even born, it’s

00:07:18.590 --> 00:07:21.000
also not clear how this ties into the Ferryman.

00:07:21.000 --> 00:07:24.979
So I think the most relevant parts of the
file are this hand drawn map, which is probably

00:07:24.979 --> 00:07:28.629
a map of the catacombs that we see The Ferryman
transform the Warrens’ laundry room and

00:07:28.629 --> 00:07:29.719
office closet into.

00:07:29.719 --> 00:07:33.130
I don’t necessarily think these catacombs
are supposed to represent a location from

00:07:33.130 --> 00:07:37.030
the real world; I was not able to find an
example of a catacomb or crypt that has this

00:07:37.030 --> 00:07:38.060
mineshaft look.

00:07:38.060 --> 00:07:41.650
But if we want to use a real location just
for comparison’s sake, I think the catacombs

00:07:41.650 --> 00:07:44.749
in Milos, Greece, which were said to have
been built during the first century of the

00:07:44.749 --> 00:07:46.289
common era, makes sense.

00:07:46.289 --> 00:07:49.699
According to the travel guide website Greeka,
“The catacombs are full of labyrinths so

00:07:49.699 --> 00:07:51.449
that the Romans could get lost in them.

00:07:51.449 --> 00:07:53.650
This was a way to protect the bodies from
their enemies.”

00:07:53.650 --> 00:07:57.490
This site makes sense as a destination associated
with Charon, because people would want their

00:07:57.490 --> 00:08:01.729
loved ones to be buried in a place where graverobbers
would not be able to easily steal the Ferryman’s

00:08:01.729 --> 00:08:02.729
toll.

00:08:02.729 --> 00:08:05.860
But I think the image most relevant to the
Warrens’ investigation is hidden behind

00:08:05.860 --> 00:08:07.729
the photo of this man with the horseshoe mustache.

00:08:07.729 --> 00:08:10.409
There’s a photo of two little girls with
their eyes closed.

00:08:10.409 --> 00:08:14.389
I think these girls may be the younger sisters
of the girl who was taken by The Ferryman,

00:08:14.389 --> 00:08:16.129
as explained by the character, Daniela.

00:08:17.466 --> 00:08:20.159
– It's this case the Warrens investigated
about this girl who was terrorized by something

00:08:20.159 --> 00:08:21.220
called the Ferryman.

00:08:21.220 --> 00:08:24.039
Here's a picture of the girl he killed.

00:08:24.039 --> 00:08:27.460
– [Zac] One of these girls could be the voice on this
audiotape in which Ed Warren interviews a

00:08:27.460 --> 00:08:29.710
young girl about the disappearance of her
sister.

00:08:29.710 --> 00:08:33.579
We hear this tape randomly start playing as
Judy Warren’s babysitter Mary-Ellen is trying

00:08:33.579 --> 00:08:34.579
to study.

00:08:34.870 --> 00:08:36.688
– [female voice] …he had silver coins
for his eyes.

00:08:36.688 --> 00:08:38.459
She said his light shows you the way to the
land of the dead.

00:08:38.459 --> 00:08:40.974
I just wanna find my sister.

00:08:40.974 --> 00:08:42.924
– [Ed] And when did she first see him?

00:08:42.924 --> 00:08:44.831
– [female voice] Not long before he took
her.

00:08:44.831 --> 00:08:48.682
She said she'd wake up, and he'd be in her
room… watching her sleep.

00:08:48.682 --> 00:08:51.635
The night she went missing, we both woke up
to a noise.

00:08:51.635 --> 00:08:54.646
It sounded like a coin falling on the floor.

00:08:54.646 --> 00:08:56.556
She told me to wait in her room.

00:08:56.556 --> 00:08:58.165
So I did.

00:08:58.165 --> 00:08:59.328
She never came back.

00:08:59.328 --> 00:09:03.169
I went to look for her and ended up in a long
hallway.

00:09:03.169 --> 00:09:04.532
Filled with coffins.

00:09:04.532 --> 00:09:05.329
Last night…

00:09:05.329 --> 00:09:06.809
I woke up to a noise.

00:09:06.809 --> 00:09:08.754
Another coin being dropped.

00:09:08.754 --> 00:09:10.597
It was like he was…

00:09:10.597 --> 00:09:12.876
Like he was calling me.

00:09:12.876 --> 00:09:14.529
– [Ed] Have you ever seen the Ferryman?

00:09:14.529 --> 00:09:18.348
– [female voice] If you don't pay his toll,
he'll take your soul.

00:09:18.813 --> 00:09:22.604
It sounds as if The Ferryman broke one of
his rules and came after a girl who was still

00:09:22.604 --> 00:09:23.346
alive.

00:09:23.346 --> 00:09:26.991
We never really get enough info to make a
definitive conclusion about why he does this,

00:09:26.991 --> 00:09:28.834
but I came prepared with a theory.

00:09:28.834 --> 00:09:32.380
When I explained the history of The Ferryman’s
various depictions in culture across time,

00:09:32.380 --> 00:09:36.070
we saw the deity becoming more and more Grim
Reaper like, with the Annabelle Comes Home

00:09:36.070 --> 00:09:39.740
version sporting a nose indent like you would
see on a skull and wearing something similar

00:09:39.740 --> 00:09:40.740
to the reaper’s cloak.

00:09:40.740 --> 00:09:44.899
If we look at versions of a Grim Reaper in
other cultures, a common theme is that interfering

00:09:44.899 --> 00:09:47.100
with death’s design can result in death.

00:09:47.100 --> 00:09:51.100
The big one to come to mind is Final Destination,
where certain characters have clairvoyant

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:54.410
visions, allowing them to escape their death,
but death continues to come for them in other

00:09:54.410 --> 00:09:55.660
ways until they succumb.

00:09:55.660 --> 00:09:59.990
I actually did a Horror History episode on Death in Final
Destination, if you are interested.

00:09:59.990 --> 00:10:04.040
In Japanese culture, Gods of death are known
as Shinigami, and there’s a fantastic series

00:10:04.040 --> 00:10:05.810
about them known as Death Note.

00:10:05.810 --> 00:10:10.180
In Death Note, if one Shinigami tries to extend
the life of a human whose lifespan has expired,

00:10:10.180 --> 00:10:11.240
that Shinigami will die.

00:10:11.240 --> 00:10:14.190
This is the only known way to kill a Shinigami.

00:10:14.190 --> 00:10:17.529
Perhaps one of these sisters somehow saved
the life of their older sister, who was supposed

00:10:17.529 --> 00:10:19.140
to die, and is now being punished.

00:10:19.140 --> 00:10:22.121
There’s nothing in the movie to back up
this theory, but it seems like this may have

00:10:22.121 --> 00:10:25.370
been the original idea based on the content
of this deleted scene.

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:29.790
In it, Mary-Ellen explains that when she was
five years old, she got really sick and almost

00:10:29.790 --> 00:10:30.790
died.

00:10:30.790 --> 00:10:34.649
– I came so close to dying, I didn’t feel
anything.

00:10:34.649 --> 00:10:38.100
– And she is actually the only character in
the movie that The Ferryman goes after.

00:10:38.100 --> 00:10:41.670
I think he’s targeted her because she was
supposed to die when she was five years old,

00:10:41.670 --> 00:10:45.029
but perhaps because the Warrens had already
captured the Ferryman inside this coin pouch,

00:10:45.029 --> 00:10:47.639
he was not able to take her from the land
of the living.

00:10:47.639 --> 00:10:48.839
Until… he was released.

00:10:48.839 --> 00:10:50.670
It all started in 1968.

00:10:50.670 --> 00:10:54.731
The Warrens had just investigated the case
of a supposedly possessed doll named Annabelle,

00:10:54.731 --> 00:10:58.320
and they decided to take the doll and keep
it in their cursed artifact room for safe

00:10:58.320 --> 00:10:59.320
keeping.

00:10:59.320 --> 00:11:02.170
On the way home, their car broke down outside
of a cemetery and they discovered that other

00:11:02.170 --> 00:11:05.129
spirits were drawn to Malthus, the demon bound
to this doll.

00:11:05.129 --> 00:11:07.320
– [Lorraine] It’s the doll, Ed.

00:11:07.320 --> 00:11:10.790
It’s a beacon for other spirits.

00:11:10.790 --> 00:11:15.339
– [Zac] The doll sat in this case until 1972, when
the Warrens were away for an evening and Mary-Ellen

00:11:15.339 --> 00:11:16.690
was babysitting for Judy.

00:11:16.690 --> 00:11:20.410
Her friend Daniela came over and snuck into
the locked room, hoping to find a way to contact

00:11:20.410 --> 00:11:21.800
her father on the other side.

00:11:21.800 --> 00:11:25.766
In doing so, she touches everything, including
the coin pouch that The Ferryman was bound in.

00:11:25.766 --> 00:11:29.759
Malthus tricks Daniela into opening the Annabelle
case and she leaves without properly locking

00:11:29.759 --> 00:11:33.430
it, so the demon simply leans the doll forward
against the glass in order to escape.

00:11:33.430 --> 00:11:36.920
Because the doll is a beacon for other spirits,
every spirit locked in that room is drawn

00:11:36.920 --> 00:11:40.029
to Malthus, who presumably, provides them
with the power to get out out of the room

00:11:40.029 --> 00:11:41.430
and terrorize the house.

00:11:41.430 --> 00:11:44.829
The Ferryman lures Mary-Ellen into The Warrens’
office using the sound of the interview tape

00:11:44.829 --> 00:11:46.399
from their investigation on him.

00:11:46.399 --> 00:11:50.040
She hears a coin drop, as one of the coin-eyed
spirits she has seen in the photograph appears

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:51.269
in the room behind her.

00:11:51.269 --> 00:11:54.870
She goes back to the hall where another coin
rolls down the stairs and lands at her feet.

00:11:54.870 --> 00:11:58.700
She picks it up and examines it to find several
slashes across the surface, as if something

00:11:58.700 --> 00:12:02.750
very powerful had scratched at it repeatedly,
hard enough to do physical damage.

00:12:02.750 --> 00:12:06.310
The Ferryman continues to roll his precious
coins in her direction, sending her on a path

00:12:06.310 --> 00:12:07.310
to the source.

00:12:07.310 --> 00:12:11.389
When she reaches the kitchen, an almost insectile
hissing sound directs her attention to the

00:12:11.389 --> 00:12:12.375
laundry room.

00:12:12.375 --> 00:12:16.794
(hissing sound)

00:12:16.794 --> 00:12:21.990
That’s when she first lays eyes on what
to this point has only been a figure of Greek

00:12:21.990 --> 00:12:23.010
legend to her.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:27.815
She locks eyes with two coins, floating near
the ceiling in the dark.

00:12:27.815 --> 00:12:29.815
(coin dropping)

00:12:32.792 --> 00:12:36.375
(suspenseful music)

00:12:36.375 --> 00:12:39.760
The positioning of The Ferryman, seemingly
perched on the ceiling, is something that

00:12:39.760 --> 00:12:42.199
we’ve seen before in the Annabelle spin-off
movies.

00:12:42.199 --> 00:12:46.220
On multiple occasions, Malthus has climbed
around on a ceiling before pouncing down on

00:12:46.220 --> 00:12:47.220
his prey.

00:12:47.220 --> 00:12:50.600
For this reason, I would assume that The Ferryman
seemingly performing the same ceiling hang

00:12:50.600 --> 00:12:55.079
trick here is a result of influence by Malthus,
whether Malthus simply taught him how to do

00:12:55.079 --> 00:12:58.769
it, or took hold of him in the same fashion
that we saw the demon Valak take hold of the

00:12:58.769 --> 00:13:00.740
the old man Bill Wilkins in the Conjuring
2.

00:13:00.740 --> 00:13:04.420
In any event, Mary Ellen is able to defend
herself by shining her flashlight at the coins,

00:13:04.420 --> 00:13:07.470
causing The Ferryman to disappear and the
coins to fall to the ground.

00:13:07.470 --> 00:13:10.930
Her flashlight dies, and she picks up one
of the coins to examine it, but as she does

00:13:10.930 --> 00:13:13.490
so, The Ferryman rushes forward, right in
front of her.

00:13:13.490 --> 00:13:17.790
Coins once again cover his eyes, and we get
a good look at his dark, dry looking face.

00:13:17.790 --> 00:13:21.620
Mary-Ellen screams and tries to run for it,
but she’s knocked to the ground by a supernatural

00:13:21.620 --> 00:13:23.899
force, then air yeeted back into the darkness.

00:13:23.899 --> 00:13:27.839
She’s only able to stop herself by grabbing
onto a door frame for dear life.

00:13:27.839 --> 00:13:31.240
At this point, The Ferryman’s powers seem
to be the standard set of abilities seen on

00:13:31.240 --> 00:13:35.440
most paranormal entities in the Conjurverse:
ability to move around quickly, climb on walls

00:13:35.440 --> 00:13:40.589
and ceilings, interact with technology, become
invisible and of course, yeet people and objects,

00:13:40.589 --> 00:13:42.490
seemingly out of thin air while invisible.

00:13:42.490 --> 00:13:45.899
But his next move is not something we’ve
really seen from other creatures.

00:13:45.899 --> 00:13:50.019
The Warrens’ laundry room is instantly transformed
into the catacombs and spirits with token

00:13:50.019 --> 00:13:54.680
eyes appear in coffins on each side of him
as he raises a warm, dim lantern up around

00:13:54.680 --> 00:13:55.680
his face.

00:13:55.680 --> 00:13:59.121
Like the illusion Daniela experiences, where
she appears to be stabbed by a knife, this

00:13:59.121 --> 00:14:02.910
room transformation is only visual, and the
house would return to normal after Mary-Ellen’s

00:14:02.910 --> 00:14:06.230
flashlight comes back to life and she shines
it in Charon’s direction.

00:14:06.230 --> 00:14:09.850
The Ferryman retreats to the closet in Ed
and Lorraine’s office, but not before retrieving

00:14:09.850 --> 00:14:12.950
the Annabelle doll, which the girls would
need to return to it’s case to have any

00:14:12.950 --> 00:14:16.420
hope of stopping the horrors wrecking havoc
around the house.

00:14:16.920 --> 00:14:17.920
– Annabelle.

00:14:17.920 --> 00:14:19.219
The doll.

00:14:19.219 --> 00:14:21.290
She’s the one who’s doing all of this.

00:14:21.290 --> 00:14:25.449
– When they arrive, The Ferryman creaks open
the closet door to give them a peak and reveal

00:14:25.449 --> 00:14:27.959
Annabelle, then slam it shut before they can
get to it.

00:14:27.959 --> 00:14:31.240
They’re able to locate the key, but when
Mary-Ellen reopens the door, the closet has

00:14:31.240 --> 00:14:33.690
transformed into the catacombs of the Ferryman.

00:14:33.690 --> 00:14:36.960
At the end of the corridor, Mary-Ellen sees
the girl that the Ferryman killed, the one

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:40.279
that looks just like her, eyes covered and
holding the Annabelle doll.

00:14:40.279 --> 00:14:44.740
It was a trap to coax her further into the
crypt, but she had no choice but to venture

00:14:44.740 --> 00:14:45.930
forward to retrieve the doll.

00:14:45.930 --> 00:14:46.930
Her lamp goes out.

00:14:46.930 --> 00:14:50.519
This is the second time Mary-Ellen’s source
of light was extinguished in The Ferryman’s

00:14:50.519 --> 00:14:54.920
presence, and it makes me wonder if the infernal
deity named for intense light, as the son

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:58.569
of night and darkness has some ability to
manipulate light sources.

00:14:58.569 --> 00:15:02.130
She is unable at first to pry the doll from
her doppelganger’s grasp.

00:15:02.130 --> 00:15:03.980
The girl comes to life and Screams.

00:15:03.980 --> 00:15:04.765
(scream)

00:15:04.765 --> 00:15:08.060
Although we don’t see exactly how Mary-Ellen
gets ahold of the doll, she is able to grab

00:15:08.060 --> 00:15:11.670
it and throw it forward to Judy, and she’s
only able to scream for her to go.

00:15:11.670 --> 00:15:15.129
After Judy and Mary-Ellen try to return the
doll, Malthus uses its power to prevent them

00:15:15.129 --> 00:15:19.050
from closing the encasing, and The Ferryman,
along with the other spirits released into

00:15:19.050 --> 00:15:20.720
the house close in on them.

00:15:20.720 --> 00:15:23.880
But with Daniela’s help, they’re able
to close the door, and The Ferryman and all

00:15:23.880 --> 00:15:27.750
the other threats that Malthus released that
evening are contained once more.

00:15:27.750 --> 00:15:29.509
– The evil is contained.

00:15:29.509 --> 00:15:32.941
– Could we see the Ferryman return in another
Conjurverse movie?

00:15:32.941 --> 00:15:35.810
I mean maybe, he’s technically, like, still
there.

00:15:35.810 --> 00:15:38.250
If Malthus gets out again, anything could
happen.

00:15:38.250 --> 00:15:40.040
But no, let’s be real that’s not gonna
happen.

00:15:40.040 --> 00:15:43.639
To fully understand the lore behind Malthus
and the rest of of the evil deities in the

00:15:43.639 --> 00:15:45.920
Conjurverse, you need to click that playlist
on the left.

00:15:45.920 --> 00:15:50.089
But first, remember to subscribe to CZsWorld
for new horrors every week, ring the deathbell

00:15:50.089 --> 00:15:53.750
and select all notifications and I will see
you in the next video.

00:15:53.750 --> 00:15:55.000
Assuming we both survive.

00:15:55.200 --> 00:15:58.401
(somber music)

